{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "An order of the ancient Knights Radiant, among the most graceful fighters, who preferred to serve as medics or rescue trapped allies.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Edgedancers use the Surges of Abrasion and Progression.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Some felt that the Edgedancers ignored important things and thought them small-minded.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "72" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "They follow a philosophy of remembering the ordinary people of the world, and tend to ignore high society.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "36" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The ancient Radiants",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "72" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Though renowned for their deadliness, Edgedancers preferred to serve as medics or to rescue trapped allies. They were among the most graceful of the Radiants, in battle and out.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "72" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the Radiants abandoned Urithiru, the Edgedancers were too busy relocating the city's servants and farmers to leave a message in the gem archive.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "72" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They sometimes served as scouts, or joined special teams with Windrunners and Skybreakers.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The refounded order",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Wyndle is the first spren of his kind known to bond someone since the Recreance, choosing Lift.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The Ideals",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "19" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "An Edgedancer must reach the Third Ideal before their spren can become a Shardblade.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "19" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Powers",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Abrasion lets them manipulate friction. They are said to \"ride the thinnest rope at speed, dance across rooftops, and move through a battlefield like a ribbon on the wind.\"",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Progression lets them make plants and other organic things grow much faster than normal, and heal.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
